      "writtenOn": "2021-02-10T00:01:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What I meant is that you can store vma-\u003evm_ops instead of vma-\u003evm_ops-\u003eopen and vma-\u003evm_ops-\u003eclose separately.\n\nOn L176 you copy the content of the vma-\u003evm_ops and then later you override some of the callbacks. By doing dmabuf-\u003evma_orig_ops \u003d vma-\u003evm_ops; you save the pointer to the original ops, so dmabuf-\u003evma_orig_ops-\u003eopen() and dmabuf-\u003evma_orig_ops-\u003eclose() will be pointing to the original callbacks. This way instead of having two pointers in the struct dmabuf (dmabuf-\u003evma_open and dmabuf-\u003evma_close) you can have only one (dmabuf-\u003evma_orig_ops).",
      "parentUuid": "3181210f_05ea78db",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 179,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 180,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "ae1ee2f9eb1f2bc4c8ac0a514bcc471c152c06e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
